// @run
// @log 8
// The SHARPEST cell of D-ISALIAS, isolated: `type Id = i32` — the transparency arm that has
// been in the compiler longest — used as a union ARM and narrowed with `is` builds an
// INVALID MODULE on the parent commit (`failed to compile: wasm[0]::function[4]`). No
// diagnostic, no reject: a module wasmtime refuses to compile.
//
// Nothing about arrays or functions is involved. `canonEmitTypeNames` rewrote the union's
// member `Id` to `i32` and left the `is Id` spelling alone, so the emitter resolved no
// variant for the test and emitted code it could not validate. The defect was reachable
// from the oldest arm of the rule the whole time; the array arm (D-ALIASARR) merely made it
// impossible to keep missing, because the array arm's own checker reject had been hiding it.
//
// Kept separate from `transparent-alias-is-narrow-union-arm.vl` (which pins all four arms
// together) because that file goes red on the parent for the ARRAY arm's checker error
// first — a lid over this one, exactly the pattern method note 78 describes.
type Id = i32

const a: Id | string = 7
if a is Id {
  print(a + 1)
}
